# RACE Stage 1 aggregate per-sequence rows: 117.5 MiB, above the GitHub 100 MiB
# per-file limit. The file is not lost. It is the byte-exact concatenation, in the
# frozen Stage 0 workload order, of the ten committed
# stage1_prediction/results/full/checkpoints/<workload>/per_sequence_results.jsonl
# files, and re-running stage3_residency/stage1_prediction/scripts/run_stage1_full.sh
# rebuilds it from those checkpoints without repeating any simulation. Its SHA-256
# 5b4fdc8089be00d8c54c2eb70fc4604be281659ad02316afc349f47c6a5360c2 stays recorded in
# the sealed Stage 1 archive manifest, so the reconstruction is verifiable.
stage3_residency/stage1_prediction/results/full/per_sequence_results.jsonl
